# Cloudflare Pages URL rewrites / redirects
#
# Architecture: all boat pages live under /boats/<slug>. The /boats/
# prefix keeps the catchall from matching root-level assets (css/js/
# images) as it did when we tried /:slug on the root.
#
# Rules evaluate top-to-bottom; first match wins. Static files
# (favicon.ico, falka.css, /falka-images/*, etc.) are served first.

# --- Legacy 301s: pre-rename slugs and old un-prefixed URLs ---
# Keep this list growing only for slugs that existed in the wild —
# there's no automatic way to enumerate them. New boats added in
# Sanity get a /boats/<slug> URL from day one and don't need any
# legacy entry.

/falka-01        /boats/vika-8           301
/falka-03        /boats/vika-81          301
/vika-8          /boats/vika-8           301
/falka-02        /boats/falka-02         301
/falka-02-open   /boats/falka-02-open    301
/vika-81         /boats/vika-81          301

# --- Extension-less HTML files ---
# The files are served directly at /login and /boat (with
# Content-Type from _headers). These 301s catch old bookmarks.
/login.html      /login                  301
/boat.html       /boat                   301

# --- All boat pages ---
# Catchall under /boats/ is safe: root-level asset paths like
# /falka-cms.js and /falka.css don't match because they're not
# under /boats/. Slug is extracted from the URL by falka-cms.js
# to fetch the right boat from Sanity.
/boats/:slug     /boat                   200
